      "before": "a1-u01-d04-e01",
      "title": { "en": "ł" },
      "body": { "en": "*Ł* sounds like the English w in \"water\", so *miło* is \"MEE-wo\". Remember that the Polish letter *w* is said like v." }
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u01-d04-t02",
      "before": "a1-u01-d04-e07",
      "title": { "en": "Two spellings, one sound" },
      "body": { "en": "*Ch* and *h* are the same sound, a strong h: *słucham*, *halo*. *Ó* and *u* are also the same sound, like the oo in \"boot\" but shorter: *wieczór*. Only the spelling differs, just as with *rz* and *ż*." }
    }
  ],
